WEBVTT

00:00:36.625 --> 00:00:38.750
Another day of nice weather.

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:42.708
Nothing beats peace
and quiet, all right.

00:00:55.083 --> 00:00:57.917
What is this?!

00:00:57.958 --> 00:01:01.000
<i>I can hear my heart bell</i>

00:01:01.000 --> 00:01:03.583
<i>What could it mean?</i>

00:01:03.583 --> 00:01:07.292
<i>A bell in my heart is ringing</i>

00:01:08.708 --> 00:01:13.000
"Heaven's Lost Property"

00:01:13.083 --> 00:01:18.833
<i>It all started way back then </i>
<i>(ringin' ringin')</i>

00:01:18.833 --> 00:01:24.417
<i>Ever since before we were born</i>
<i>(ringin' ringin')</i>

00:01:24.417 --> 00:01:29.667
<i>you were destined to appear out of nowhere,</i>

00:01:29.667 --> 00:01:32.667
<i>right before my eyes,</i>

00:01:32.667 --> 00:01:35.458
<i>I'm sure of it</i>

00:01:35.458 --> 00:01:41.125
<i>My wishes and ambitions and daydreams</i>

00:01:41.125 --> 00:01:46.792
<i>take me to an unknown level and knock on a door</i>

00:01:46.792 --> 00:01:53.000
<i>You give me the key and the future</i>
<i>I need to take flight (with your wings)</i>

00:01:53.000 --> 00:01:55.917
<i>I can hear my heart bell</i>

00:01:55.917 --> 00:01:58.958
<i>There's no stopping it</i>

00:01:58.958 --> 00:02:04.625
<i>It's a sign, rung by an angel, saying "I love you"</i>

00:02:04.625 --> 00:02:07.500
<i>Can you hear my heart bell?</i>

00:02:07.500 --> 00:02:09.833
<i>What could it mean?</i>

00:02:09.833 --> 00:02:15.250
<i>A bell in my heart that I've </i>
<i>never heard before is ringing</i>

00:02:15.250 --> 00:02:24.375
<i>But even so, you don't suspect a thing</i>

00:02:30.500 --> 00:02:35.083
Good day, ladies and gentlemen.
My name is Sugata Eishiro.

00:02:35.083 --> 00:02:38.167
This is my assistant, Pretty II.

00:02:39.000 --> 00:02:42.000
In the decades following 1280,

00:02:42.000 --> 00:02:46.500
the world experienced
a great boom in trading.

00:02:46.500 --> 00:02:49.792
The thing that made this possible
was the magnetic compass.

00:02:49.792 --> 00:02:53.417
However, long before the
use of the mariner's compass,

00:02:53.417 --> 00:02:57.000
people followed migratory birds and fish,

00:02:57.000 --> 00:02:59.208
and sailing routes were well established.

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:04.667
Apparently, continents were even discovered,
thanks to the movements of birds and fish.

00:03:04.667 --> 00:03:06.958
The magnetic compasses
possessed by animals

00:03:06.958 --> 00:03:09.208
have immeasurable potential.

00:03:09.208 --> 00:03:13.833
Go, Pretty! Use your compass,
and show us a New World!

00:03:19.792 --> 00:03:23.375
I should have cooked and eaten her right off.

00:03:24.750 --> 00:03:27.417
"Love and Triangles, Revisited"

00:03:27.833 --> 00:03:30.583
W-Why are all these panties here?

00:03:30.583 --> 00:03:34.542
I do not know.
Could they be like migratory birds?

00:03:34.542 --> 00:03:36.417
Migratory birds?

00:03:38.500 --> 00:03:40.500
Ah, these panties are...!

00:03:45.708 --> 00:03:49.292
So, does that mean the panties
from back then have returned?

00:03:49.292 --> 00:03:53.917
Yes. They must have circled
all the way around the globe.

00:03:53.917 --> 00:03:55.500
All the way?

00:03:55.500 --> 00:04:00.292
It is possible that they came home
because they missed you, Master.

00:04:00.292 --> 00:04:04.292
You came all the way
back here, just to see me?

00:04:11.000 --> 00:04:13.000
Oh, you guys!

00:04:15.250 --> 00:04:16.500
--Tomo...

00:04:16.500 --> 00:04:19.250
--<i>Yikes, I have to get out of here, now!</i>
--Tomo...

00:04:21.167 --> 00:04:23.333
Why are so many pairs of my panties...

00:04:23.333 --> 00:04:26.292
...here in your room, Tomo?!

00:04:26.292 --> 00:04:29.042
--Tomo, you sicko!
--W-Wait!

00:04:36.458 --> 00:04:40.208
What... What an awful thing to happen...

00:04:40.208 --> 00:04:43.667
Look at this, Sohara!
Look at all these panty remains!

00:04:43.667 --> 00:04:47.042
You've taken their bright future from them!

00:04:47.042 --> 00:04:50.792
--No, Master, the card's effect simply wore off.

00:04:50.792 --> 00:04:54.792
--Whatever, just throw them all away, okay?
--No, Master, the card's effect simply wore off.

00:04:54.792 --> 00:04:57.750
I never want to go through
anything like last time again!

00:04:57.750 --> 00:04:59.792
Yeah, you can count on me!

00:05:00.250 --> 00:05:04.125
Geez, Tomo, it's hard to put any trust in you.

00:05:06.000 --> 00:05:08.833
I know. Say, Ikaros...

00:05:11.625 --> 00:05:13.792
Yes, there are.

00:05:16.542 --> 00:05:18.625
<i>All right!</i>

00:05:18.625 --> 00:05:20.833
What? They returned?

00:05:20.833 --> 00:05:23.000
Yes. When I got up this morning,

00:05:23.000 --> 00:05:25.208
the panties came flying back in a flock.

00:05:25.208 --> 00:05:28.000
Hmm, that's fascinating.

00:05:28.000 --> 00:05:32.000
There are stories of New Worlds
being found by following birds.

00:05:32.000 --> 00:05:33.000
--By assuming the direction the underwear flew off in as alpha,

00:05:33.000 --> 00:05:35.292
--So then,
--By assuming the direction the underwear flew off in as alpha,

00:05:35.292 --> 00:05:39.292
--Sakurai, you have a large number of panties at your house?
--and their course as beta, the computational formula...

00:05:39.292 --> 00:05:41.292
--Uh, yes.
--What?

00:05:41.292 --> 00:05:46.208
--There are many panties, both used and unused, of various colors,
--This computational formula... it couldn't be... a New World...?

00:05:46.208 --> 00:05:49.583
now flying around the room of a
wholesome young man like yourself?

00:05:49.583 --> 00:05:51.083
They aren't flying now.

00:05:51.083 --> 00:05:55.958
And among them is the pair
that Miss Mitsuki wore, as well?

00:05:56.833 --> 00:06:02.958
Sakurai, you are a boy, and all.
I won't ask anything further.

00:06:02.958 --> 00:06:05.958
Tomo, you <i>did </i>throw them all away, right?

00:06:05.958 --> 00:06:07.208
You promised!

00:06:07.208 --> 00:06:09.667
Yeah, you can count on me.

00:06:09.667 --> 00:06:12.125
<i>I can't trust him at all!</i>

00:06:13.292 --> 00:06:17.958
Tomo, did you throw away
all those panties from yesterday?

00:06:17.958 --> 00:06:20.208
Hey, Tomo, are you there?!

00:06:20.208 --> 00:06:21.917
Do you hear me?!

00:06:21.917 --> 00:06:23.792
Yes, I threw them out.

00:06:23.792 --> 00:06:25.792
Well, okay then.

00:06:27.875 --> 00:06:29.500
<i>The hell I did!</i>

00:06:29.500 --> 00:06:33.333
<i>I am at the prime of my puberty,</i>
<i>the prime of my youth!</i>

00:06:33.333 --> 00:06:37.167
<i>There's no way I'm gonna get</i>
<i>rid of an item as nice as these.</i>

00:06:45.458 --> 00:06:48.250
W-What was that?!

00:06:48.250 --> 00:06:52.792
A-ha. Tomo, I <i>knew </i>you didn't throw them away.

00:06:52.792 --> 00:06:53.958
Sohara!

00:06:53.958 --> 00:06:59.500
Ikaros had the perfect card
for me, so I had her help me out.

00:06:59.500 --> 00:07:02.917
Those panties are going to... explode.

00:07:02.917 --> 00:07:04.667
It's like this--

00:07:04.667 --> 00:07:08.083
Tomo, every pair of panties
you look at will explode.

00:07:08.083 --> 00:07:09.375
Then, that pair just now...

00:07:09.375 --> 00:07:13.708
Mm-hmm. I'm thinking that maybe
this will mend your sicko ways.

00:07:14.625 --> 00:07:17.208
The effect will last all day long,

00:07:17.208 --> 00:07:20.042
and only when you're inside your house, Tomo.

00:07:20.042 --> 00:07:22.708
But even at that,
I'll bet you haven't thrown out

00:07:22.708 --> 00:07:25.417
a single pair out of all those panties, right?

00:07:26.000 --> 00:07:29.833
I'm going out with Ikaros today.

00:07:29.833 --> 00:07:34.042
Tomo, good luck trying
to get out of your house.

00:07:34.042 --> 00:07:34.542
--Bye.

00:07:34.542 --> 00:07:36.375
--W-Wait, Sohara!
--Bye.

00:07:36.917 --> 00:07:38.500
Learned your lesson?

00:07:38.500 --> 00:07:45.000
No. There's some kind of huge
bug that landed on the wall in your room.

00:07:45.000 --> 00:07:48.833
You're kidding! Where?! Where?!

00:07:48.833 --> 00:07:51.667
Tomo, where is it? Huh?

00:07:57.542 --> 00:07:59.375
Fool.

00:07:59.375 --> 00:08:01.792
You've got a habit of opening
your window while changing,

00:08:01.792 --> 00:08:04.917
thinking I can't look
through the window at you.

00:08:04.917 --> 00:08:05.375
--You've always been so predictable.

00:08:05.375 --> 00:08:10.583
--Tomo, you idiot! You perv! I hate you! We're through!
--You've always been so predictable.

00:08:13.250 --> 00:08:15.917
Okay, let's go, Ikaros.

00:08:15.917 --> 00:08:18.208
But, what about Master?

00:08:18.208 --> 00:08:21.042
Never mind him, we're going out without him.

00:08:21.958 --> 00:08:25.833
<i>You mean, I have to watch out,</i>

00:08:25.833 --> 00:08:29.125
<i>or any panties I look at</i>
<i>are going to become bombs?</i>

00:08:29.125 --> 00:08:33.000
<i>That rotten Sohara! Puberty</i>
<i>is a time to see, sniff, and slip over!</i>

00:08:33.000 --> 00:08:35.000
<i>What a terrible thing to pull on me!</i>

00:08:35.000 --> 00:08:39.292
<i>In any case, I have to get out</i>
<i>of this house as soon as possible.</i>

00:08:41.667 --> 00:08:44.375
<i>I hung them all up yesterday, huh?</i>

00:08:51.375 --> 00:08:54.250
<i>Oh, no. I could die from all this.</i>

00:08:54.250 --> 00:08:57.125
<i>I seriously have to think of a way out!</i>

00:08:57.125 --> 00:09:02.542
<i>Hold on. As long as I don't look</i>
<i>at them, they won't explode, right?</i>

00:09:03.792 --> 00:09:06.167
<i>Hey, that was easy. </i>

00:09:06.167 --> 00:09:09.875
<i>Even if I can't see, it's still my</i>
<i>own house. This will be a cinch!</i>

00:09:09.875 --> 00:09:13.708
<i>All right, I'll just zip down</i>
<i>the stairs to the first floor.</i>

00:09:18.167 --> 00:09:21.375
<i>I can't touch them, either?!</i>

00:09:21.375 --> 00:09:24.292
<i>In that case,</i>
<i>I'll escape through the window!</i>

00:09:31.208 --> 00:09:33.583
<i>That's right, yesterday,</i>
<i>I decorated the whole house,</i>

00:09:33.583 --> 00:09:35.875
<i>as though it were Christmas.</i>

00:09:45.167 --> 00:09:46.542
<i>What's the use?</i>

00:09:46.542 --> 00:09:50.542
<i>First thing I'll do is head into</i>
<i>the bathroom, and calm down.</i>

00:09:53.083 --> 00:09:55.583
<i>Aw... man...</i>

00:09:58.958 --> 00:10:03.208
"Heaven's Lost Property"

00:10:08.417 --> 00:10:09.542
What's the matter?

00:10:09.542 --> 00:10:12.083
I think Master is in trouble.

00:10:12.083 --> 00:10:15.917
It's okay. Tomo has to learn his lesson.

00:10:19.000 --> 00:10:23.042
Ah, look! How cute!

00:10:23.042 --> 00:10:25.458
These have angel wings on them.

00:10:25.458 --> 00:10:27.917
They'd be perfect for you,
wouldn't they, Ikaros?

00:10:29.917 --> 00:10:32.250
Come to think of it, Ikaros,

00:10:32.250 --> 00:10:34.792
you've only got the underpants
that Tomo bought for you

00:10:34.792 --> 00:10:39.833
at the convenience store, don't you?
That won't do. You're a girl.

00:10:39.833 --> 00:10:42.292
You can't be left to
Tomo's perverted tastes.

00:10:43.208 --> 00:10:46.542
I'll pick out some
first-rate cute things for you.

00:10:46.542 --> 00:10:50.250
It will be my present,
for letting me borrow your card.

00:10:59.250 --> 00:11:01.250
Mm-hmm, perfect.

00:11:05.833 --> 00:11:11.292
Ikaros, by any chance,
is this your first time in a place like this?

00:11:11.292 --> 00:11:15.000
You've never gone shopping or
anything with your friends before?

00:11:15.000 --> 00:11:16.625
Friends?

00:11:20.208 --> 00:11:23.958
I do not have friends.

00:11:25.375 --> 00:11:30.000
Oh. Ikaros...

00:11:30.000 --> 00:11:35.042
I, um, er... I'm sorry for asking.

00:11:36.292 --> 00:11:41.083
When I first moved here,
I was all alone, too.

00:11:41.083 --> 00:11:44.792
So I know just how you feel.

00:11:44.792 --> 00:11:51.500
When I was little, I wasn't
very strong, so I couldn't go outside.

00:11:51.500 --> 00:11:54.958
At the time, only Tomo,
the boy who lived next door,

00:11:54.958 --> 00:11:58.000
was friends with me.

00:11:58.000 --> 00:12:00.042
He would bring caterpillars to my room,

00:12:00.042 --> 00:12:02.292
and eat my snacks without asking.

00:12:02.292 --> 00:12:04.292
He was kind of a mess,

00:12:05.125 --> 00:12:08.125
but I was really glad on my birthday.

00:12:18.542 --> 00:12:22.583
So this is where you are.
What's the matter, Sohara?

00:12:22.583 --> 00:12:27.417
When people have birthdays,
they call lots of their friends over,

00:12:27.417 --> 00:12:30.500
and have a birthday party, right?

00:12:31.750 --> 00:12:37.042
Today is my birthday, but I'm all alone.

00:12:45.875 --> 00:12:46.625
Hey.

00:12:46.625 --> 00:12:47.833
Tomo!

00:12:47.833 --> 00:12:50.000
This is yummy.

00:12:50.000 --> 00:12:55.625
That's the birthday cake
my mom bought for me.

00:12:56.833 --> 00:12:59.917
Happy birthday, Sohara.

00:12:59.917 --> 00:13:02.500
I know. You can have this.

00:13:02.500 --> 00:13:06.125
It's a <i>hassaku </i>orange seed
my grandpa gave me yesterday.

00:13:06.125 --> 00:13:10.792
If you plant this, you'll have
lots of <i>hassaku </i>oranges, every year.

00:13:10.792 --> 00:13:13.208
Nice, huh?

00:13:13.208 --> 00:13:15.042
Mm-hmm...

00:13:19.375 --> 00:13:21.708
"Sohara"

00:13:24.500 --> 00:13:26.750
That sure takes me back.

00:13:26.750 --> 00:13:30.208
Tomo has always had that side to him.

00:13:31.250 --> 00:13:34.875
Appearances aside,
he's sensitive to others' feelings,

00:13:34.875 --> 00:13:39.750
genuinely kind,
and surprisingly dependable...

00:13:39.750 --> 00:13:44.458
Oh, but really, he's usually
an idiot and a sicko!

00:13:46.375 --> 00:13:51.708
Tomo would never say it,
but he's concerned about you, Ikaros.

00:13:54.583 --> 00:14:00.667
And I'm your friend, too.
You're not alone anymore, okay, Ikaros?

00:14:06.333 --> 00:14:08.750
Master is in trouble.

00:14:09.958 --> 00:14:13.375
Yeah, I am a bit worried about him.

00:14:13.375 --> 00:14:16.375
Maybe we should be
getting back home to him, huh?

00:14:20.083 --> 00:14:22.667
Now to make a frontal charge to the door!

00:14:35.750 --> 00:14:41.042
Just a little farther to the goal!

00:14:47.292 --> 00:14:49.375
W-What the...!?

00:15:09.708 --> 00:15:12.500
Huh? Am I...

00:15:12.500 --> 00:15:13.458
Are you all right?

00:15:13.458 --> 00:15:16.083
Shake it off, Sakurai.

00:15:16.083 --> 00:15:18.625
Sugata, what are you guys...?

00:15:18.625 --> 00:15:21.417
We heard what happened from Ikaros.

00:15:21.417 --> 00:15:24.625
We came to investigate the
underwear in question,

00:15:24.625 --> 00:15:26.458
but had no idea it had come to this.

00:15:26.458 --> 00:15:28.708
It was a real ordeal, huh?

00:15:28.708 --> 00:15:32.958
Did I... manage to make it outside?

00:15:33.875 --> 00:15:35.875
I made it!

00:15:36.958 --> 00:15:39.625
Huh? Where's Sohara?

00:15:39.625 --> 00:15:41.667
Inside the house.

00:15:41.667 --> 00:15:46.500
It appears that she was blown
into the house by that explosion.

00:15:46.500 --> 00:15:48.125
She what?!

00:15:50.458 --> 00:15:52.625
It's my fault.

00:15:52.625 --> 00:15:56.375
It's because I looked at
her panties that Sohara is...

00:15:56.375 --> 00:16:03.167
Go on, Sakurai. You are the only
one who can save Mitsuki.

00:16:03.167 --> 00:16:04.583
Yes, ma'am.

00:16:05.583 --> 00:16:07.042
Here.

00:16:08.167 --> 00:16:10.125
W-What the...?

00:16:10.125 --> 00:16:13.958
There are times when a boy must fight.

00:16:13.958 --> 00:16:17.625
You have to be the one to finish the job

00:16:17.625 --> 00:16:20.333
in the house of fun that you built.

00:16:24.625 --> 00:16:26.125
All right.

00:16:30.958 --> 00:16:33.792
Sakurai Tomoki will be right back!

00:16:35.875 --> 00:16:39.167
Just sit tight, Sohara!

00:16:39.167 --> 00:16:40.417
Master...

00:16:40.417 --> 00:16:43.458
If anyone other than Tomoki went in,

00:16:43.458 --> 00:16:45.292
there wouldn't be any explosions, right?

00:16:45.292 --> 00:16:51.958
I am well aware of that.
But it's much more fun this way, isn't it?

00:16:52.750 --> 00:16:55.417
Same old Mikako as ever.

00:16:58.542 --> 00:17:01.292
Sohara! Where are you?!

00:17:01.292 --> 00:17:02.583
Sohara!

00:17:02.583 --> 00:17:04.417
No! Stay back!

00:17:06.583 --> 00:17:08.000
Why are you running away?!

00:17:08.000 --> 00:17:11.542
Thanks to you, my panties
have been blown away!

00:17:11.542 --> 00:17:14.542
Right now, I'm not wearing
anything down below!

00:17:18.083 --> 00:17:20.208
What was that?! I couldn't hear you!

00:17:20.208 --> 00:17:22.208
I can't take any more!

00:17:22.875 --> 00:17:25.167
Wait, Sohara!

00:17:28.625 --> 00:17:30.875
<i>Oh, no! Inside my room is...</i>

00:17:32.083 --> 00:17:35.375
Sohara! Whatever you do,
don't open my closet!

00:17:35.375 --> 00:17:38.833
That's where my cutie collection is!

00:17:40.042 --> 00:17:43.625
What is... all this...?

00:17:43.625 --> 00:17:48.000
Sohara, run! There's a trap
set in there to protect my goodies!

00:17:50.500 --> 00:17:52.125
I can't see!

00:17:53.792 --> 00:17:55.167
W-What?!

00:17:55.167 --> 00:17:58.167
It's what I worked so hard to build last night--

00:17:58.167 --> 00:18:00.833
my goodie collection guardian,

00:18:00.833 --> 00:18:04.458
the Super-Fusion Panty-Robo!

00:18:06.583 --> 00:18:08.292
"Super-Fusion Panty-Robo"

00:18:09.167 --> 00:18:10.500
Sohara!

00:18:10.500 --> 00:18:11.792
Let me go!

00:18:11.792 --> 00:18:15.333
<i>If I'm going to save Sohara,</i>
<i>I'll have to face those panties.</i>

00:18:15.333 --> 00:18:20.333
<i>But if those panties explode now,</i>
<i>Sohara could get hurt.</i>

00:18:20.333 --> 00:18:22.333
<i>What should I do?</i>

00:18:23.458 --> 00:18:24.500
<i>Tomo...</i>

00:18:24.500 --> 00:18:27.417
<i>That voice-- it's Grandpa!</i>

00:18:32.000 --> 00:18:34.833
What happened? You're hurt.

00:18:36.667 --> 00:18:40.208
I ran into some trouble with my lady.

00:18:41.458 --> 00:18:43.083
Grandpa...

00:18:44.583 --> 00:18:49.417
Listen here, Tomo.
Listen to what Grandpa has to say.

00:18:49.417 --> 00:18:53.083
You're a man, too.
Someday, you'll find someone

00:18:53.083 --> 00:18:56.250
who you'll be head-over-heels for.

00:18:56.250 --> 00:19:01.083
But... in time,
she may bare her fangs at you.

00:19:01.083 --> 00:19:03.917
When she does, what will you do?

00:19:05.375 --> 00:19:12.208
Turn your back and run away?
No, you won't, Tomo.

00:19:12.208 --> 00:19:16.833
<i>Thank you, Grandpa.</i>
<i>You've opened my eyes.</i>

00:19:19.208 --> 00:19:21.667
Save me, Tomo!

00:19:33.250 --> 00:19:34.250
Tomo!

00:19:34.250 --> 00:19:39.083
<i>That's it, Tomo!</i>
<i>Embrace that which you love,</i>

00:19:39.083 --> 00:19:41.792
<i>as much as you can!</i>

00:19:45.833 --> 00:19:47.458
<i>Show us...</i>

00:19:49.250 --> 00:19:52.292
<i>...what you're made of!</i>

00:19:52.292 --> 00:19:55.958
Brave Pants In!!

00:20:13.292 --> 00:20:14.333
Is he dead?

00:20:14.333 --> 00:20:16.375
He may well be.

00:20:18.833 --> 00:20:20.833
Master is...

00:20:34.083 --> 00:20:36.750
<i>This battle is over.</i>

00:20:43.750 --> 00:20:45.292
Sohara...

00:20:45.292 --> 00:20:47.333
Tomo...

00:20:47.333 --> 00:20:51.083
Thank you. You saved me.

00:20:51.083 --> 00:20:55.542
No, this was all my fault. I'm sorry.

00:21:06.125 --> 00:21:09.417
Tomo, you sicko!

00:21:27.958 --> 00:21:40.042
<i>All men everywhere are silent soldiers</i>

00:21:41.750 --> 00:21:47.208
<i>A life lived to die happily</i>

00:21:47.208 --> 00:21:54.083
<i>is all that we need</i>

00:21:54.083 --> 00:22:01.042
<i>Ah, don't open your eyes</i>

00:22:01.042 --> 00:22:07.917
<i>Ah, my beautiful one</i>

00:22:07.917 --> 00:22:14.750
<i>I don't want you to see me</i>

00:22:14.750 --> 00:22:21.667
<i>forcing myself to turn my back on you</i>

00:22:22.875 --> 00:22:28.375
<i>Never in my life has it been so hard</i>

00:22:28.375 --> 00:22:36.250
<i>to part with someone</i>

00:22:40.583 --> 00:22:43.542
"The night before"
♪ Pantser Break! ♪

00:22:44.000 --> 00:22:49.500
Remember, your mission
is to defend my porno collection.

00:22:49.500 --> 00:22:52.333
Be sure not to let anyone find them.

00:23:02.958 --> 00:23:05.917
Now then, off to bed.

00:23:12.917 --> 00:23:18.167
I didn't send you the angel for this to happen.

00:23:18.167 --> 00:23:19.958
I'm sorry.

00:23:19.958 --> 00:23:23.500
It looks like you could
get caught up in this, as well.

00:23:23.500 --> 00:24:08.171
You've been found out.
